| Severity | Count | Top Issue |
|----------|-------|-----------|
| 🟡 Moderate | 4 | Oversized struct + missing `readonly` + ToString allocations |
| ℹ️ Info | 1 | Culture-aware string search in format parsing |

**Top recommendation for your dashboard scenario:** Make it a `readonly struct` storing only `Bits`, compute the rest on demand, and rewrite `ToString()` to use `stackalloc`/`TryFormat`. This shrinks the struct from 48→8 bytes and eliminates per-call GC allocations — critical when formatting thousands of values per second.

